---
import DocsLayout from '../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import { commands } from '../data/site';
---
<DocsLayout title="Commands and permissions" description="RedstoneLimiter commands, in-game GUI controls, permissions, statistics, notifications, chunk whitelist and quarantine actions.">
<div class="page-head"><div class="eyebrow">REFERENCE / ADMINISTRATION</div><h1 class="page-title">Commands & permissions</h1><p class="lead">The main command is <code>/redstonelimiter</code>. You can use the shorter <code>/rl</code> or <code>/redstone</code> aliases.</p></div>
<section><h2>Command reference</h2><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Command</th><th>Action</th><th>Permission / restriction</th></tr></thead><tbody>{commands.map(([command,meaning,permission])=><tr><td><code>{command}</code></td><td>{meaning}</td><td>{permission}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div><p class="small-note"><code>/rl menu</code> also works as a compatibility alias of <code>/rl gui</code>.</p></section>
<section class="prose"><h2>How the control panel works</h2><p>Open <code>/rl gui</code> in game. The GUI shows active chunks and blocks, plus controls for whitelist, manual quarantine, presets, and limits.</p><div class="grid-2"><article class="card"><span class="mini-label">CHUNK VIEW</span><h3>Inspect a problem</h3><p>Click a chunk to view its individual active blocks. Shift-left-click a chunk to toggle its whitelist policy. Shift-right-click to toggle manual quarantine.</p></article><article class="card"><span class="mini-label">LIMITS VIEW</span><h3>Tune thresholds</h3><p>Change enabled state, maximum activations, duration, sustain and sliding mode separately for each scope. Block Max opens a dedicated per-material limits page.</p></article></div><div class="callout"><strong>Quarantine is manual only.</strong> It does not happen automatically when redstone activity exceeds a configured max. Quarantine also takes precedence over whitelist. <a href="/how-it-works/#diagram-05-chunk-policy">Watch the animated chunk-policy explanation →</a></div><h2>Permission nodes</h2><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Node</th><th>Default</th><th>Purpose</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>redstonelimiter.admin</code></td><td>OP</td><td>Open and operate the control panel</td></tr><tr><td><code>redstonelimiter.stats</code></td><td>OP</td><td>View statistics</td></tr><tr><td><code>redstonelimiter.reload</code></td><td>OP</td><td>Reload plugin configuration</td></tr><tr><td><code>redstonelimiter.notify</code></td><td>OP</td><td>Receive and toggle notifications (default configured node)</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>The notification permission is configurable via <code>notifications.permission</code>. Cross-server travel requires extra setup; it is disabled by default.</p></section>
</DocsLayout>
